From 3ccc0a4ead1cfdd37f8c67c9c000ae416dd80cdd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mlgprorektm8 <67933lance@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 04:03:14 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] FIX-180: native vertex mirrors reach 256 KB past their range

Lance's "vertex sky explosions" in Tokyo: for single frames, in bursts, the
world geometry (buildings, road, walls) went missing and the sky colour showed
through over the windshield (fences, lights, wipers still drew). Counted with
a probe of the presented picture (FIX-175): 6-19 such frames in a 450 s race,
none in the tunnels with RYGT_NATIVE_MIRRORS=0, none with index-only mirrors,
still there with vertex-only mirrors.

Mirrors (NAT-150) now reach 256 KB past the range they are made for (within
the mapping; RYGT_NATIVE_MIRROR_SLACK=<KB>, 0 as before). The same race then
has no such frame in 15,887 at 57.5 fps (47-51 fps before), with ~290 larger
mirrors instead of ~800. The exact cause is still open: mirror contents matched
guest memory on the CPU side (FIX-176) and right before draws on the GPU side
(FIX-179), no sampled draw read past its V#s (FIX-181), and keeping CPU-written
mirrors, keeping mirrors away from regions and dropping the vertex shortcut
did not help.

Diagnosis switches added on the way (all off by default):
- FIX-175 RYGT_NATIVE_WATCH_DISPLAY=x,y,w,h: thirds of a rectangle of each
  presented picture, one line a frame; FIX-182 saves frames that get much
  darker than the one before (user\log\glitch_*.raw).
- FIX-176 RYGT_NATIVE_MIRROR_VERIFY=<MB a frame>: guest memory under mirrors
  hashed per 64 KB granule, changes without a CPU write fault logged.
- FIX-177 RYGT_NATIVE_MIRRORS=v|i: only vertex or only index ranges mirrored.
- FIX-178 RYGT_NATIVE_VERTEX_NEAR=0: no OPT-004 attribute shortcut.
- FIX-179 RYGT_NATIVE_MIRROR_CHECK=<n>: every n-th mirror bind copied out
  with guest memory right before the draw and compared.
- FIX-181 RYGT_NATIVE_VERTEX_REACH_CHECK=<n>: highest vertex/instance a draw
  reads against its V#s and mirrors.
- FIX-183 RYGT_NATIVE_DRAW_BARRIER=1, FIX-184 RYGT_NATIVE_MIRROR_NODROP=1,
  FIX-185 RYGT_NATIVE_MIRROR_REGION_GAP=<KB>.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
